              "answer": "Take |f| (reflect the part below the x-axis), then the reciprocal: vertical asymptotes at \\(x=1\\pm\\sqrt5\\) (zeros of f), horizontal asymptote y = 0, local minimum \\(\\left(1,\\frac15\\right)\\) from the vertex, y-intercept \\(\\frac14\\); the graph is always positive, rising to infinity at both asymptotes.",
